@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.pattern.progressively_expandable_table a ds:Pattern;
    ds:name "Progressively Expandable Table";
    ds:summary "Progressively Expandable Table composes a Canonical `ModularTable` with an optional title and a footer that reports the loaded count. When the caller has loaded fewer rows than the effective total, the footer offers one action to load up to five more rows. The separately exported footer can instead label that action “View all” and can place a caller-supplied secondary action before the count.\n\nUse this pattern for a bounded preview where rows are appended in place or where a compact table links into a complete collection. The component does not fetch data, increase a limit, navigate, announce newly loaded rows, or provide loading and error states; the parent owns those behaviors through `onLimitChange` and updated props.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.pattern.expandable_table\n  role: progressively expandable table\n  description: Composes a loaded table subset with count and disclosure controls.\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: table introduction\n        name: Title\n        description: Renders a string as a styled paragraph or renders a supplied React element unchanged.\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"0..1\"\n          slotName: title\n          condition: Rendered when title is a string or a valid React element.\n    - node:\n        uri: global.component.modular-table\n        role: tabular data region\n        name: Modular Table\n        description: Renders the supplied columns and currently loaded rows.\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        role: count and disclosure assembly\n        name: Expandable Table Footer\n        description: Presents an optional secondary action, result count, and one disclosure action.\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: secondary command\n              name: Additional action\n              description: Renders caller-supplied footer content before the count and disclosure group.\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                slotName: additionalCta\n                condition: Rendered when additionalCta is provided.\n          - node:\n              role: static collection summary\n              name: Result count\n              description: Reports the displayed count against the effective total.\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                condition: Rendered when the effective total is greater than zero.\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.button\n              role: more-results command\n              name: Disclosure action\n              description: Requests more rows or a transition to all rows.\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                condition: Rendered when itemCount is less than the effective total.\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=17-24&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 44\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n**Incrementally reveal rows**\n\nShow an initial table subset and let users append a small batch in place. Keep the caller’s limit increment consistent with the label, which never promises more than five rows.\n\n**Offer a full-list transition**\n\nCompose `ExpandableTableFooter` directly with `viewAll` when a compact table or adjacent content transitions to the complete collection. `ExpandableTable` itself does not expose `viewAll`.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Navigate stable pages**\n\nNumbered pages or prev/next navigation through a result set.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using progressive expansion when users need traditional page navigation.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use Table Pagination instead for multi-page result sets.\n\n**Load an unbounded feed**\n\nAn unknown-length feed where repeated expansion is the primary browsing mode.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using the footer to incrementally load an unknown total count.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a purpose-built infinite scroll or virtual list component when totals are unknown.\n\n**Represent asynchronous state**\n\nLoading and error states that the component should display.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Relying on the footer to signal loading or error conditions.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Pair the table with separate loading and error notifications, and prevent duplicate requests by managing pending state in the caller.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- Use descriptive column headers and preserve table semantics.\n- Pass a heading element through `title` when the table needs to appear in the page outline. A string title is a styled `<p>`, not a semantic heading or table caption.\n- Treat the count as static text. It is not a live region, so announce appended results elsewhere when immediate assistive-technology feedback is required.\n- Give `additionalCta` an accessible name and avoid duplicating the disclosure action’s purpose.\n\n### Content\n\n- Use concrete singular and plural nouns so the count reads naturally.\n- Keep any additional CTA distinct from “Show N more” or “View all”.\n- Current visible templates are hard-coded English. Localize “Showing”, “of”, “Show N more”, and “View all” before using this implementation in a translated surface.\n\n### Internationalization / globalization\n\n- `itemNames` supports only one singular and one plural form and `pluralize(..., \"exact\")`; it is not a complete plural-rules API.\n- The component does not format numbers with `Intl.NumberFormat`. Format requirements and translated sentence order need an upstream API rather than preformatted numeric props.\n- Keep the maximum batch label of five synchronized with localized copy and actual caller behavior.\n\n### Device\n\n- Provide responsive cell content or a scroll treatment when columns cannot fit narrow screens.\n- The footer uses a flex row with the expansion block pushed to the end and no component-owned wrap rule. Verify long translations and `additionalCta` content at narrow widths.\n\n### Keyboard\n\n- Keep disclosure and additional actions as native controls in a predictable tab order.\n- After loading more, retain focus on the disclosure control unless navigation occurs.\n- Prevent repeated activation while a request is pending; the component has no loading or disabled prop of its own.\n- `onLimitChange` is called synchronously with no event or requested limit. The component does not catch callback errors or reconcile the label with the caller’s actual increment.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.columns`";
        ds:summary "React Table column definitions passed to `ModularTable`. ";
        ds:propertyType "list of objects";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `Column<T>[]`, where `T extends Record<string, unknown>`. Each column must define headers and cells that remain meaningful at the available width. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "ExpandableTable.data";
        ds:summary "Currently loaded row records passed to `ModularTable`. ";
        ds:propertyType "list of objects";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `T[]`, where `T extends Record<string, unknown>`. This is the rendered subset, not necessarily the complete result set. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.itemNames`";
        ds:summary "Nouns used by the footer's count text.";
        ds:propertyType "object";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `{ plural: string; singular: string }`. Supply forms that read correctly after an exact number; no locale or grammar service is invoked. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.onLimitChange`";
        ds:summary "Handles activation of the disclosure button.";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `() => void`. The component does not pass the next limit, await a result, disable itself, or distinguish loading from navigation. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.totalCount`";
        ds:summary "Reported total before `hasNoMoreItems` adjustment. ";
        ds:propertyType "number";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Keep nonnegative and aligned with the same result scope as `data`. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.additionalCta`";
        ds:summary "Content composed at the start of the footer.";
        ds:propertyType "node";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `ReactNode`. It is rendered without validation or decoration; supply an accessible control or noninteractive content appropriate to this position. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.getCellProps`";
        ds:summary "Adds props to each rendered table cell.";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `(cell: Cell<T>) => Partial<TableCellProps & HTMLProps<HTMLTableCellElement>>`. Preserve table semantics and header relationships. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.getRowProps`";
        ds:summary "Adds props to each rendered table row.";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `(row: Row<T>) => Partial<TableRowProps & HTMLProps<HTMLTableRowElement>>`. Adding row activation requires equivalent keyboard behavior and an accessible name. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.hasNoMoreItems`";
        ds:summary "Replaces the effective total with `itemCount`. ";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Omission is treated as false. Use only when the data source establishes that no further rows exist; this can override a larger stale `totalCount`. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.itemCount`";
        ds:summary "Count used by footer calculations when it differs from `data.length`. ";
        ds:propertyType "number";
        ds:defaultValue "`data.length`";
        ds:constraints "Keep synchronized with the rows represented to users. Values above the effective total are clamped in count copy but suppress the disclosure action. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTable.title`";
        ds:summary "Optional table introduction.";
        ds:propertyType "node";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `ReactNode`. Numbers and other non-element nodes accepted by the type are ignored; pass a semantic heading when needed. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.itemCount`";
        ds:summary "Loaded or represented item count.";
        ds:propertyType "number";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Keep nonnegative and synchronized with visible content. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.itemNames`";
        ds:summary "Nouns used in count copy.";
        ds:propertyType "object";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `{ plural: string; singular: string }`. Supply grammatically correct exact-count forms. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.onLimitChange`";
        ds:summary "Handles the disclosure action.";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `() => void`. Own loading prevention and state changes in the caller. ";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.totalCount`";
        ds:summary "Reported complete count.";
        ds:propertyType "number";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Represents the same result scope as `itemCount`. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.additionalCta`";
        ds:summary "Content before the footer's count group.";
        ds:propertyType "node";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Exact type: `ReactNode`. Keep subordinate to the disclosure action and provide its own semantics. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.className`";
        ds:summary "Additional class on the footer root.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Do not remove the flex relationship required by the count group. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.hasNoMoreItems`";
        ds:summary "Uses `itemCount` as the effective total.";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Omission is treated as false. Set only after confirming the end of the result set. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`ExpandableTableFooter.viewAll`";
        ds:summary "Replaces “Show N more” with “View all”.";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "Omission is treated as false. This changes copy only; the callback must perform the full-load or navigation behavior. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ].
